ation, anchors from the replay), then prepares sources for the new entry only. The shared finish then takes one fresh root inventory, quotes the remainder with forecastArchiveFinish using the real anchor count, and admits only when canSpend(remaining + 65,536 metadata) holds. A refusal goes through the existing finish-affordability capacity wake. The legacy anchors go into buildOwnedPass, and from there into replayInput.\n- Shared code. The published fixed path is unchanged in order and guard. It now calls the same finish with anchor count 0, which is the same computation as before.\n- No double work. The old range is prepared once, inside planLegacyArchiveAnchors, and the new entry once. The witness's order list shows exactly target, sources:plan, prepare:0 to cutoff, prepare:first.\n- The anchor bit. It is set only by confirming a publication, which this head does not change. The witness shows it absent after bootstrap, after the refused quote, after the pending Mark and after a lost read-back, and present only after confirmation. Later appends then make no old reads.\n\nSecurity: no new authority. No bound, price, finish formula, margin, deadline, Mark, CAS or frontier comparison changes. Migration work stays charged to the pass's own budget. A refused quote creates no Mark, mint or send; the witness asserts mintCalls and sendCalls are 0 there. Only the module's own validation can produce the legacy anchors: the entry points refuse supplied ones, and missing, pruned or unsupported old inputs still refuse through the existing validator. The two seals were refreshed after the gate flagged the change, and I reviewed the code they cover above.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. Sharing the fixed finish between the published and legacy paths avoids a second quote implementation. One nonblocking note: planRootFixedUnpublishedArchivePass repeats most of the guard that planRootFixedLegacyArchivePass checks again. One guard list would be enough.\n\nWitness and control, verified by me from the records:\n- The two new cases (cutoffs 0 and 1) use actual Native birth, entries, SQLite rows, frontier bootstrap, eviction and pending reconstruction. The policy, source, target, HTTP and token ports are test stand-ins, as the note says.\n- The cases force a real capacity wake (a lower entry ceiling, with wake capacityDeferrals 1). They then refuse a complete quote under a 512 KiB metadata limit at finish-affordability, with 65,536 reserved and no Mark, mint or send. Then they plan exactly one next entry with every axis of actual cost within used + remaining and within ARCHIVE_BOUNDS, at 46 of 64 nodes. The pending Mark carries the legacy anchors and is rebuilt after advance and eviction; confirmation sets anchorsPublished.\n- In the control 3b1e043a (on ed44e966), only the old predicate is restored. Both new cases fail with fixedFinish null, refused at scout-next by the adaptive path, and the four older cases still pass (Tests 2 failed | 4 passed).\n\nMerge and hygiene. The head merges onto Main 2aaba5e4 with no conflict. Main has not changed packages/scope or the seal file since 86204d44. git diff --check is clean. All five commit subjects are 63 characters or fewer, and the note is 10.5 KB.\n\nLimits, stated plainly: the local quote does not show a fit on the hosted Worker. The hosted rows refused one node short at the adaptive scout, and this head moves them to a path the local witness prices at 46 of 64 nodes; the hosted figure is still unmeasured. The RefcountedCanceler / abortContextSignal diagnostics in the native output are recorded, not explained.\n\nRollout notes for the planner (nonblocking):\n1. Deploy dap-grow with --keep-vars. The three rows already have a deferral count above 0, so their next capacity wake (at most 300 s later) takes the new path.\n2. In the tail, a working pass shows fixedFinish on the pass line, then a pending Mark, then confirmed with anchorsPublished true. If a refusal at finish-affordability still shows a nodes shortfall, record the quote's components and stop, as the note says; do not raise the bound.\n3. Directory is confirmed at seq 1 and Site lane and Destination at seq 0, the two cutoffs the witness covers.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head a3f7332b / tree f7733877. The builder lands; the planner deploys.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:71ad2b84975d36db8c18ded3c67ed5cdd428db90","binding":"assigned","head":"a3f7332b0933952d7a41634706732cd0ac09429e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d42c28db5ddab073b39c28e380b322f184bb7f9c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc394fd55240ca0c17f228d8bad439ab68ba7ecb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ab7bd75bec64858c9a0d13b60fdd3103ce4ca1d7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}